  "question": {
    "text": "The 'spin only' magnetic moment value of \\(\\mathrm{MO}_4{ }^{2-}\\) is _______ BM. (Where M is a metal having least metallic radii. among \\(\\mathrm{Sc}, \\mathrm{Ti}, \\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{Cr}, \\mathrm{Mn}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Zn}\\) ).\n(Given atomic number: \\(\\mathrm{Sc}=21, \\mathrm{Ti}=22, \\mathrm{~V}=23, \\mathrm{Cr}=24, \\mathrm{Mn}=25\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Zn}=30\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Metal having least metallic radii among $\\mathrm{Sc}, \\mathrm{Ti}, \\mathrm{V}$, $\\mathrm{Cr}, \\mathrm{Mn} \\& \\mathrm{Zn}$ is $\\mathrm{Cr}$.\nSpin only magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{CrO}_4^{2-}$.\nHere $\\mathrm{Cr}^{+6}$ is in $\\mathrm{d}^0$ configuration (diamagnetic).",
    "image": null
  },
